1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,260
Listen to a talk on a podcast about psychology.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,166
Podcast Host:

3
00:00:04,166 --> 00:00:07,307
Did you see that new thriller movie that came out last week?

4
00:00:07,307 --> 00:00:09,180
I did and loved it.

5
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,932
The action, the plot twists… I was totally captivated.

6
00:00:12,932 --> 00:00:14,600
Time just flew by.

7
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:20,020
Not a single thought occurred to me that was unrelated to the movie.

8
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:25,099
What I experienced is what psychologists call hard fascination.

9
00:00:25,099 --> 00:00:29,050
Hard fascination means intense focus and concentration.

10
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:35,042
Whether it’s TV programs, video games… hard fascination is all too easy to come

11
00:00:35,042 --> 00:00:37,040
by in this modern world.

12
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:41,260
There’s another type of fascination—soft fascination.

13
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:46,612
There’s still effortless attention, meaning that no special effort is required for you to

14
00:00:46,612 --> 00:00:47,326
stay focused,

15
00:00:47,326 --> 00:00:50,180
but there’s still room for other thoughts.

16
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:53,912
When I take a walk in the park and look at the flowers

17
00:00:53,912 --> 00:00:57,932
and trees, for example, I might be thinking in the back of my mind

18
00:00:57,932 --> 00:00:59,080
about my dinner plans.

19
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:04,210
Now, one thing to know is hard fascination causes mental fatigue.

20
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:09,060
The mind is so intensely focused that it gets tired fast.

21
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,202
What follows mental fatigue?

22
00:01:11,202 --> 00:01:16,020
You might find yourself easily distracted, irritable, and stressed.

23
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:22,570
Soft fascination, in contrast, engages a different part of the brain—the DMN,

24
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:24,585
or Default Mode Network,

25
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:29,120
which soothes the mind and helps combat mental fatigue.

26
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:34,202
So next time you feel like your mind is on overload, turn off the

27
00:01:34,202 --> 00:01:36,017
TV, put down your phone.

28
00:01:36,017 --> 00:01:37,106
Take a walk,

29
00:01:37,106 --> 00:01:40,010
or simply sit and stare at the clouds.
